# No archive manager and no text editor natively. file-roller had NO unique dependency tail
# (app-arch/libarchive is held by flatpak/systemd/gvfs/samba/ostree and app-arch/gnome-autoar
# by gnome-shell+nautilus, so both stay) and nautilus already compresses and extracts through
# gnome-autoar, which covers the common case. gnome-text-editor was the sole consumer of a
# 12-package tail — gtksourceview, libspelling, enchant, hunspell, editorconfig-core-c and the
# seven app-dicts/myspell-* dictionaries that hunspell PDEPENDs per L10N (myspell-de alone is
# ~10 MB compressed) — and app-editors/nano stays in the image for console editing.
# Both are one click away in GNOME Software (org.gnome.FileRoller, org.gnome.TextEditor);
# deliberately NOT in FLATPAK_PREINSTALL, because either would pull org.gnome.Platform
# (~1.07 GB installed) into a 4 GiB /var that already carries Firefox on the freedesktop
# runtime — a net loss over the ~50 MB of native tail this removes from the read-only root.
